+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-21-validate-task-input/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Why
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, so odd tasks get in: blank or huge titles, unknown priorities, empty or spaced tags. The list should refuse them with a clear error.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Adding, renaming and tagging validate their input and return an `invalid-input` error saying what is wrong.
+- Rejected: a title empty or only spaces; a title over 120 characters (after trimming); a priority not `low`, `normal` or `high`; a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+- A rejected call changes nothing in the list (no task, no id issued, no timestamp).
+- New error code `invalid-input` in `TodoErrorCode`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-input-validation`: rules for acceptable titles, priorities and tags.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/domain/task.ts` (validators), `src/domain/list.ts` (`add`, `rename`, `tag`), `src/domain/result.ts` (error code), tests. Callers must handle the new error code; no API signature changes.
